MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_001: This is far enough. Thank you for accompanying me.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_002: Oh, am I off the clock now? Then can I ask you\nsomething?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_003: That was sudden. But no matter—speak your mind.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_004: Queen Theodora, my job is to, like, fight alongside\nyou in the Heroic Games, right?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_005: My job is to, like, take down as many enemies as\nI can on the battlefield, right?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_006: Doesn't feel like bodyguarding you when you go out\nis in the job description.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_007: So you are refusing guard duty?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_008: Nah, if you want me to do it, I'll do it. Not like I'm\nin any position to refuse.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_009: It's just, y'know, extra work. I thought maybe I could\nget some extra pay for it.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_010: So it's a question of compensation?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_011: When I do unpaid overtime, my heart just isn't in it.\nYou get me?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_012: Although maybe you wouldn't, being queen and all.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_013: Very well. I shall approve a bonus. Look for an\nenvoy to deliver it later.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_014: Awesome! You're the best, Queen Theodora.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_015: Hmph. You have more backbone than I am\naccustomed to in a soldier.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_016: Oh. Am I about to get chewed out?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_017: No, I simply hadn't heard your sentiment expressed\nbefore. I shall bear it in mind for all my soldiers.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_018: Ah, gotcha.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_019: It can be challenging for a queen to truly hear the\nvoices of those who serve her. Even those like you—
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_020: Hey, that's another thing. I'm not getting paid to\nhang out with you, am I?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_021: And you said a minute ago that we'd gone "far\nenough" for guard duty.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_022: Hm. True enough.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_023: In that case, I'm out. See you around.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_C_024: A backbone is a noble quality in a soldier, but I do\nwonder if she takes it too far...
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_001: Hm? Who's the queen talking to?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_002: Your Majesty, please see reason! That woman must\nnot be allowed to remain at your side!
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_003: She is the daughter of Tabatha, one of Dyan's\ncronies who turned his bow against you!
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_004: Are they...talking about me?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_005: Your Majesty stripped their estate from them.\nSurely they still hold a grudge against you.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_006: She may have hidden ties to Dyan. For all we know,\nshe sought this position in order to get revenge.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_007: Unbelievable. Haaah... It never ends.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_008: You are mistaken. If revenge were her motive, she\nhas had ample opportunity to take it.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_009: Yes, she is somewhat eccentric. That is simply\nher being true to herself.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_010: More importantly, in my view, she is an eminently\nskilled warrior.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_011: I am? I mean, I am! But I had no idea Queen\nTheodora knew it.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_012: But that could all be an act! She could be biding her\ntime, waiting to bare her fangs.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_013: So it is my judgment that is at fault. Is that what\nyou have come to tell me?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_014: You are dismissed.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_015: She's been keeping an eye out...and she's seen\nthe real me.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_016: What are you doing there? Eavesdropping?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_017: AAH! Uh, um. Yeah, I guess I was.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_018: Tell me, Lilian. Do you resent me?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_019: Huh? Where is this coming from?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_020: I punished those who sided with Dyan during\nhis attempted coup.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_021: Your father's sentence was the forfeiture of his rank\nand property. I seized your home.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_022: Yet here you are, serving me. Not as a conscript\nbut as a volunteer. Why?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_023: Well, I don't see the point in resenting you. And I\ncan't afford to care what people think of me.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_024: My plan is to save up lots of money and buy back\nour estate one day.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_025: So...rather than dwell on the past, you look forward.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_026: I mean...I don't know what my dad would say about\nall of it.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_027: He always insisted that Prince Dyan should be the\none on the throne.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_028: I heard it every day growing up.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_029: Dyan colluded with outsiders to murder our father.\nHe attempted to drag our country into civil war.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_030: There is no justification or forgiveness for such\nbehavior. It is wrong on its face.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_031: Dyan attempted to drag our country into civil war.\nSuch behavior is unbecoming of a king.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_032: My late father, the previous king, bade me to be\nstrong. To love and care for my subjects.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_033: Just as Yu Phas did. I have lived my life steering by\nthat oath.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_034: That is why I sit on the throne and Dyan was\nexpelled. Do you understand, Lilian?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_035: Yeah. I get where you're coming from.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_036: You are one of my subjects—I love and care for you\ntoo. Your house and your faction are not your worth.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_037: Take pride in yourself as my retainer, Lilian Tabatha.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_038: Yeah...I'll do that.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_B_039: As long as you're looking out for me, Queen\nTheodora...I think I got this.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_001: You called for me? Am I here to get paid or get\nchewed out?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_002: Rejoice, Lilian. I have a reward in honor of your\nhard work.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_003: I intend to return your estate to you.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_004: Huh? Seriously? Like, the WHOLE estate?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_005: Yes. You have distinguished yourself in my service,\nboth as a soldier and a personal guard.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_006: As queen, I would be remiss not to reward you.\nOrdinarily, I would grant silver, gold, or weaponry.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_007: But you have expressed to me a desire for something\nunlike the usual prizes.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_008: My...my house... I'm finally gonna get it back?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_009: Just like that?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_010: Is something wrong? Should you not be overjoyed?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_011: It's just...uh. It's weird to think about getting it back\nso suddenly.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_012: Too abrupt to believe, is it? Then I shall invite its\ncurrent owner here to settle the issue.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_013: Nah, that's OK. I mean, I appreciate the offer.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_014: But I'd rather work hard to save up and buy the\nplace back myself.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_015: Are you certain? This was your long-held dream.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_016: How can I put this? It's not just about getting\nthe property back.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_017: It's that...like...I don't feel like I'm done working\nfor you yet.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_018: Sorry, what was that?
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_019: I wanna earn it back on my own. So, thanks but\nno, thanks.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_020: I see. You've no shortage of insolence to reject a\ngift from your queen.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_021: Oh...here's that chewing out, I guess.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_022: Perish the thought. But while you're being insolent,\ntell me what you would rather have.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_023: Well, that pile of silver and gold you mentioned\nsounds pretty good.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_024: Oh, and can I get a raise? Then I'd be psyched to\nwork even harder.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_025: Hah! Very well. All of this shall be yours.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_026: Thank you, Queen Theodora! For you, I'll do my\nvery best!
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_027: Truly? Ah...I see. A joke.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_028: No, no, I wasn't kidding. I really am with you all\nthe way.
MID_SE_Seo_Lil_A_029: I'll keep you safe if it kills me. That's the kind of\nloyalty money can't buy!